  "intro": [
    "Santa Teresa sits on the southern tip of the Nicoya Peninsula, a long stretch of beach backed by jungle with famous surf and a bohemian crowd. Dirt roads, small hotels and open-air restaurants keep a relaxed feel, though it has become more upmarket in recent years.",
    "Waves attract surfers from around the world, with breaks for all levels. The area also offers yoga, horse riding, and nearby sights such as Cabo Blanco Absolute Nature Reserve, Costa Rica's first protected area, and the waterfalls of Montezuma. Sunsets are spectacular.",
    "Nicoya is also known as one of the world's Blue Zones, where people live unusually long lives. The pace is gentle, and dust is part of the experience in the dry season. Getting here is a longer journey, but many visitors say it is worth it."
  ],
